{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"bf65edb627d9f048","type":"group","x":-340,"y":3674,"width":1060,"height":1686,"label":"4 · VALIDATE & EVALUATE"},
		{"id":"99efe58a21b19be7","type":"group","x":860,"y":2442,"width":1020,"height":1370,"label":"3A · ASSURANCE: TESTING, AUDIT & CONSTRAINTS"},
		{"id":"1474a5ea9c689263","type":"group","x":1990,"y":90,"width":320,"height":3880,"color":"5","label":"Traceability Thread"},
		{"id":"b94c2a948d45c1ce","type":"group","x":-350,"y":2442,"width":1080,"height":1142,"label":"3 · DESIGN & DE-RISK"},
		{"id":"ef970c616ec3157f","type":"group","x":-340,"y":1384,"width":1060,"height":968,"label":"2 · ANALYSE & PRIORITISE"},
		{"id":"c9825e05a87cc5f5","type":"group","x":-320,"y":548,"width":1020,"height":746,"label":"1 · DEFINE THE PROBLEM"},
		{"id":"d60a9fb4444fb8a1","type":"group","x":-300,"y":3964,"width":980,"height":584,"label":"Signal Discovery"},
		{"id":"77d72225ee089d87","type":"group","x":-320,"y":-40,"width":1020,"height":498,"label":"0 · PLAN & ENGAGE"},
		{"id":"0bfcd6404cfa9ee3","type":"group","x":-310,"y":2776,"width":1000,"height":348,"label":"Failure prompts"},
		{"id":"329a2249a1a9731e","type":"group","x":-300,"y":1524,"width":980,"height":146,"label":"Model the system context"},
		{"id":"ddf10f9367306e9f","type":"group","x":1220,"y":2630,"width":300,"height":328,"label":"Additional failure prompts"},
		{"id":"25a4b7556c0a2287","type":"group","x":-130,"y":5080,"width":640,"height":128,"label":"Reporting"},
		{"id":"7ed590a20694c2de","type":"text","text":"CONTROL TEST\nCan the project change it?\nNo → constraint, assumption or dependency","x":400,"y":1800,"width":260,"height":126},
		{"id":"1e4858262568c8ab","type":"text","text":"PRIORITISE · Lever Score\nControl (1–5) × Impact (1–5)\nTop 1–3 levers define the scope of this release","x":60,"y":1976,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"6513e608f06b0e08","type":"text","text":"CONSTRAINTS REGISTER\nBoundary conditions, assumptions and dependencies","x":400,"y":1976,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"ff1ef6cb5511db05","type":"text","text":"DELIVERABLE · PRIORITISED REQUIREMENTS\nContext model, top 1–3 levers, backlog and constraints register","x":60,"y":2132,"width":600,"height":70,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"e1d3ce3207a8c85f","type":"text","text":"AMPLIFICATION TEST\nIf changed, does the outcome move?\n→ Value driver (lever)","x":60,"y":1800,"width":260,"height":126},
		{"id":"aa880e5cfde8ed7c","type":"text","text":"ACTORS\nUsers from the stakeholder map, plus primary, secondary and administrative tools","x":-280,"y":1544,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"6fe3a0d5c8fba6e9","type":"text","text":"WALK THE AS-IS PROCESS\nWith users, trace Entry → Exit. At every hand-off, record Expected vs Observed.","x":-280,"y":708,"width":260,"height":142},
		{"id":"cf7865b6f3e51256","type":"text","text":"NARROW SCOPE (Fallback)\nIf nothing is controllable, shrink the boundary to a component the project owns.","x":-280,"y":900,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"f6ea9f6cb9bc3f83","type":"text","text":"CALM LENS · CLARIFY the Target Gap   |   BABOK: Strategy Analysis, Elicitation & Collaboration\nStrip narratives and proposed solutions until one measurable, root, in-scope gap remains.","x":-280,"y":588,"width":940,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"865343f5eaf774f6","type":"text","text":"ELIMINATION TEST\nIf removed, does the process collapse?\n→ Core requirement (protect)","x":-280,"y":1800,"width":260,"height":126},
		{"id":"d1a961ff9acf6218","type":"text","text":"BACKLOG\nRemaining requirements, ranked for later releases","x":-280,"y":1976,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"f6a0398cea075004","type":"text","text":"INPUTS\nInformation required, data sources, volumes, time and budget","x":60,"y":1544,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"ae06e083f0e1fc6f","type":"text","text":"RULES\nBusiness rules, policies, filtering and constraints, access rules, SLAs","x":400,"y":1544,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"b11186c40b47e4c1","type":"text","text":"CALM LENS · ANALYZE the Levers   |   BABOK: Requirements Analysis\nEvery requirement must name the variable it changes and how that variable closes the Target Gap.","x":-280,"y":1424,"width":940,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"edff28be414e0669","type":"text","text":"GATE 1 · Sponsor agrees the problem and scope","x":60,"y":1194,"width":600,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"51cf9e30304a3271","type":"text","text":"ELICIT ON THE 4 AXES\n- Temporal: how long, where it waits\n- Quantitative: volumes, drop-offs\n- Qualitative: errors, missing data\n- Resource: cost, effort, rework","x":60,"y":708,"width":260,"height":142},
		{"id":"06a7709f7f4f20ab","type":"text","text":"GATE 2 · Stakeholders agree priorities and constraints","x":60,"y":2252,"width":600,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"53b68d6032db4dbe","type":"text","text":"T3 · Acceptance criterion → Anti-pattern rule → Requirement\nEvery test traces to a failure it prevents","x":2020,"y":2602,"width":260,"height":106,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"15c29f9a906b39cc","type":"text","text":"T4 · Signal → Lever → Target Gap\nEach signal names the lever it measures and the gap it proves closed","x":2020,"y":3834,"width":260,"height":106,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f9fc2a68dba7f9f5","type":"text","text":"T3A · NFR → Constraint / Failure prompt → Test result → Guardrail signal\nEvery quality claim has test evidence","x":2020,"y":3018,"width":260,"height":124,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"af8a67924a1bd0d4","type":"text","text":"T2 · Requirement → Lever → Target Gap\nEvery requirement names its lever","x":2020,"y":1544,"width":260,"height":88,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"c81fce9031d14f72","type":"text","text":"DELIVERABLE · PROBLEM STATEMENT\nTarget Gap = Current state − Desired state (measurable), with in-scope and out-of-scope items","x":60,"y":1056,"width":600,"height":88,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"716abb4e2b6413fe","type":"text","text":"LIST CANDIDATE GAPS\nEvery Expected ≠ Observed becomes a candidate problem.","x":400,"y":708,"width":260,"height":142},
		{"id":"708906da06f7b73a","type":"text","text":"ROOT-CAUSE TRIAGE · Lineage Test\nTrace each gap one level upstream. Keep root gaps; record symptoms as evidence.","x":400,"y":900,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"59b5fe714bebe5fe","type":"text","text":"SCOPE TRIAGE · Sphere of Authority\nControllable → in scope. Third-party → reframe as an internal gap, or log as a dependency.","x":60,"y":900,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"a718bb234172915e","type":"text","text":"PLATEAU REACHED\nLock the setting; baseline the new process","x":60,"y":4930,"width":260,"height":88},
		{"id":"bec86946a3055b86","type":"text","text":"T1 · Target Gap ID\nBaseline measure of the current state","x":2020,"y":708,"width":260,"height":88,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"b8de2c900bbaeb46","type":"text","text":"DELIVERABLE\nBA approach, stakeholder register and system boundary","x":400,"y":330,"width":260,"height":88,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"24502a0267fca83a","type":"text","text":"MAP STAKEHOLDERS\n- Sponsor / business owner\n- Primary users (interface, API submission point)\n- Secondary users (consume outputs)\n- Administrative users\n- Tool and data owners","x":60,"y":120,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"e3e88339d12bd7f8","type":"text","text":"RECEIVE REQUEST\nLog the request as stated. Treat it as a symptom or a proposed solution, not yet as the problem.","x":-280,"y":120,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"5b234efe5f90629f","type":"text","text":"DEFINE THE BASELINE CONTRACT\n- Entry and Exit points\n- Trigger events\n- Documented SLAs and target metrics","x":400,"y":120,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"09c788c61daa1bbf","type":"text","text":"T0 · Request ID\nOriginal request and stakeholders recorded","x":2020,"y":120,"width":260,"height":88,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"fc5d78686db058aa","type":"text","text":"CALM LENS · Set the boundary first   |   BABOK: Business Analysis Planning & Monitoring\nNo gap can be measured until Entry, Exit and the Baseline Contract are known.","x":-280,"y":0,"width":940,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"bb4962b5225d94d9","type":"text","text":"OUTPUT · SIGNAL REGISTER\nPrimary and guardrail signals, with baselines and thresholds","x":400,"y":4404,"width":260,"height":124,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8d26dc0682c437df","type":"text","text":"8 · CONFIRM WITH DATA OWNER\nCheck the data is available, reliable and can be reported","x":60,"y":4404,"width":260,"height":124},
		{"id":"271ca7eee250a3a3","type":"text","text":"DESIGN UAT / PILOT · R.I.P. Test\n- Reversible: rollback is planned\n- Isolated: one lever per test\n- Proximal: signal visible quickly","x":60,"y":4618,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"164144165783e59f","type":"text","text":"PHASED ROLLOUT · Gradient\nPilot group → wider group → full rollout; compare the signal at each step","x":400,"y":4618,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"46caec388112461f","type":"text","text":"7 · SPECIFY EACH SIGNAL\nName, formula, data source, owner, baseline, target, minimum meaningful change, window, frequency","x":-280,"y":4404,"width":260,"height":124},
		{"id":"0ac05c5c7c256334","type":"text","text":"READ THE SIGNAL\nCompare the result with the Target Gap baseline","x":60,"y":4774,"width":260,"height":126},
		{"id":"f3fd69a2519fb7b1","type":"text","text":"DEGRADED / NO SIGNAL\nAdjust the lever, or return to Stage 2 (or Stage 1 if the gap was wrong)","x":-280,"y":4774,"width":260,"height":126},
		{"id":"08d85e7932b7c2c9","type":"text","text":"6 · ADD GUARDRAIL SIGNALS\nFrom Stage 3 failure modes and constraints: up to 3 measures that must not worsen","x":-280,"y":4194,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"8dac6b97b1064ed1","type":"text","text":"2 · TRACE THE LEVER PATH\nFor each top lever, walk Lever → first state change → Target Gap metric. Find where the effect shows first.","x":60,"y":3984,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"856b2531ab92b2a9","type":"text","text":"3 · LIST CANDIDATE SIGNALS (4 axes)\n- Temporal: cycle time, wait time\n- Quantitative: volumes, conversion, drop-off\n- Qualitative: error rate, data completeness\n- Resource: cost, effort, rework","x":400,"y":3984,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"4aaee57669eb3794","type":"text","text":"4 · SIGNAL VIABILITY FILTER\n- Measurable from an existing data source?\n- Attributable to one lever?\n- Visible within a short window?\n- Baseline stable enough to show a real change?","x":400,"y":4194,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"25ea777b3f2c78b8","type":"text","text":"5 · SELECT (Max-3)\nOne primary signal per lever. Prefer the earliest viable signal; keep the gap metric as the outcome check.","x":60,"y":4194,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"bfac0897c662a023","type":"text","text":"CALM LENS · MEASURE the Signal Delta   |   BABOK: Solution Evaluation\nProve the gap has closed with evidence; never assume it from delivery alone.","x":-280,"y":3714,"width":940,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"64a5224a314037d9","type":"text","text":"DEFINE THE SUCCESS SIGNAL\nFind and define the evidence that will prove the Target Gap has closed. Follow the signal discovery steps below.","x":-280,"y":3834,"width":940,"height":70},
		{"id":"c33372ed012625d8","type":"text","text":"1 · ANCHOR TO THE TARGET GAP\nThe Stage 1 gap metric is the outcome signal. Record its current and desired values.","x":-280,"y":3984,"width":260,"height":160},
		{"id":"c32214de1dafeeb7","type":"text","text":"GATE 3 · Design sign-off\nBusiness owner, IT, and Compliance / Legal review where applicable","x":60,"y":3474,"width":600,"height":70,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"580255810c2fbeff","type":"text","text":"Misuse & Invalid Inputs","x":-280,"y":2882,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"ac0614a079d3e247","type":"text","text":"Null & Partial States","x":60,"y":2882,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"43ff89809e5fe546","type":"text","text":"CHANGE & TRANSITION PLAN\nData migration, training, rollout sequence, rollback plan","x":400,"y":3160,"width":260,"height":146},
		{"id":"f55219d45c9f2236","type":"text","text":"DELIVERABLE · SOLUTION REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION\nFunctional and non-functional requirements, business rules, acceptance criteria, transition plan","x":60,"y":3336,"width":600,"height":88,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"edfc24223e1e2e05","type":"text","text":"Boundary Values","x":60,"y":2958,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"1225977d365b0ef7","type":"text","text":"Idempotency & Retries","x":400,"y":2882,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"f9c9cf4b73408143","type":"text","text":"Error Visibility & Feedback","x":400,"y":2958,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"09937651b53bc23a","type":"text","text":"SPECIFY THE SOLUTION\nUser stories / functional requirements with acceptance criteria, per lever","x":60,"y":3160,"width":260,"height":146},
		{"id":"7babc3978d680b97","type":"text","text":"STILL IMPROVING\nContinue to the next rollout step","x":400,"y":4784,"width":260,"height":106},
		{"id":"86de1b28a8dd4b46","type":"text","text":"Audit Trail & Record-Keeping","x":1240,"y":2650,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"e8f19501513282e9","type":"text","text":"Data Privacy (POPIA)","x":1240,"y":2726,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"0cd749dbb7ea1ce5","type":"text","text":"Accessibility","x":1240,"y":2878,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"456d83b44225ed7b","type":"text","text":"1 · CLARIFY THE THRESHOLD\nRestate each requirement as a measurable target, e.g. 95% of responses under 3 s at peak. \"Must be fast\" is not yet defined.","x":900,"y":3264,"width":260,"height":142},
		{"id":"02d9327ebd21693a","type":"text","text":"5 · READ THE RESULTS\nCompare each result with its threshold","x":1240,"y":3456,"width":260,"height":88},
		{"id":"59ef3c1bb64611ab","type":"text","text":"OUTPUT · ASSURANCE PACK\nNFR specification, audit requirements, test results and updated register. Passed thresholds become guardrail signals.","x":900,"y":3456,"width":260,"height":124,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"94cd93fb3783f761","type":"text","text":"2 · PRIORITISE (Max-3)\nRisk = Likelihood × Impact. Focus on core components from the Elimination Test; top 3 areas get full testing, the rest lighter checks.","x":1240,"y":3264,"width":260,"height":142},
		{"id":"257116f308aba87e","type":"text","text":"WRITE ANTI-PATTERN RULES\nEach failure becomes a business rule, a non-functional requirement or an acceptance criterion","x":-280,"y":3160,"width":260,"height":146},
		{"id":"4508684e2dde3c1d","type":"text","text":"Race Conditions","x":-280,"y":2958,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c7dcba763711d290","type":"text","text":"Permission Boundaries","x":-280,"y":3034,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"6384902d6e78898e","type":"text","text":"Recovery (RPO / RTO)","x":1240,"y":2802,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"692de9d2bac351fd","type":"text","text":"CONSTRAINTS REGISTER (maintained here)\n- Regulatory: FAIS, FICA, POPIA, Companies Act\n- SLAs from the Baseline Contract\n- Access rules and technical limits\n- Each entry: source, owner, review date","x":1580,"y":2650,"width":260,"height":178},
		{"id":"7014994c470388cc","type":"text","text":"FAIL → REDESIGN\nReturn to the Stage 3 pre-mortem and future-state options","x":900,"y":3684,"width":260,"height":88},
		{"id":"f4cad86ab11e26ea","type":"text","text":"NEW CONSTRAINT FOUND\nUpdate the register; return to Stage 2 if scope changes","x":1580,"y":3684,"width":260,"height":88},
		{"id":"90c1cefd5ba28eda","type":"text","text":"CLASSIFY ANTI-PATTERN RULES\n- Functional → acceptance criteria (Specify the Solution)\n- Non-functional → NFR specification (this section)","x":900,"y":2630,"width":260,"height":248},
		{"id":"87fb2200e982f591","type":"text","text":"3 · DESIGN SCENARIOS BY INVERSION\n\"How would load, outage, misuse or bad data break this design?\" Load, stress, failover, security, privacy, audit-trail reconstruction, accessibility","x":1580,"y":3264,"width":260,"height":142},
		{"id":"930298c3fa36550b","type":"text","text":"4 · RUN TESTS (R.I.P. + Gradient)\n- Non-production, rollback ready\n- One variable per run\n- Step the load until output plateaus or degrades: the capacity limit\nRun by QA / IT; the BA validates results","x":1580,"y":3456,"width":260,"height":178},
		{"id":"2e67612af09450d0","type":"text","text":"CALM LENS · Every quality, audit and compliance need is a measurable gap with a guardrail signal   |   BABOK: Design Definition, Solution Evaluation\nNon-functional requirements are clarified as thresholds, prioritised by risk, tested by inversion and measured before sign-off.","x":900,"y":2460,"width":940,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e53a12cd3bb64877","type":"text","text":"CALM LENS · LIMIT Failure Modes   |   BABOK: Design Definition, Requirements Life Cycle\nDesign by inversion: ask how the chosen levers could break the process, then write the rules that prevent it.","x":-280,"y":2482,"width":940,"height":70,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"597d3287b25dc16b","type":"text","text":"FUTURE-STATE OPTIONS\nOne or more design options per lever, within the constraints register","x":-280,"y":2580,"width":260,"height":146},
		{"id":"157344e8c442b1ab","type":"text","text":"Out-of-Order Execution","x":-280,"y":2806,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"c8ad114faae7af64","type":"text","text":"PRE-MORTEM WORKSHOP · Bounded Inversion\n\"Using only these levers, within these constraints, how would this solution fail?\"","x":60,"y":2580,"width":260,"height":146},
		{"id":"110064fd56cee182","type":"text","text":"Scale Extremes","x":60,"y":2806,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"889728dd4cffd478","type":"text","text":"External Interruptions","x":400,"y":2806,"width":260,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"e5a324459ba9af78","type":"text","text":"NFR SPECIFICATION\n- Performance & capacity\n- Availability & recovery (RPO / RTO)\n- Security & access · Data privacy (POPIA)\n- Auditability & record-keeping\n- Usability & accessibility · Maintainability & supportability","x":900,"y":3005,"width":600,"height":222},
		{"id":"05ee361fd2f93d1c","type":"text","text":"AUDIT & RECORD-KEEPING\n- Recorded: who, what, when, before / after values\n- Retention periods as confirmed by Compliance\n- Tamper-evident and retrievable on request\n- POPIA: minimise, secure and dispose","x":1580,"y":3005,"width":260,"height":196},
		{"id":"0d1e2d6113e9446e","type":"text","text":"ELICIT CANDIDATE REQUIREMENTS\nFor each variable: what must change to close the Target Gap?","x":-110,"y":1700,"width":600,"height":70},
		{"id":"9265c3566975f84c","type":"text","text":"QUESTIONS ANSWERED\nIs the Target Gap closed? Current state vs desired state","x":-110,"y":5100,"width":260,"height":88},
		{"id":"a1ce99d08291d5f6","type":"text","text":"METRICS, DATA POINTS, DECISIONS\nSignal per lever, plateau setting, decisions taken","x":230,"y":5100,"width":260,"height":88},
		{"id":"47266ddc4ae9fd9b","type":"text","text":"DELIVERY & EXPORTS · Close-out\nFinal report, handover to operations, lessons learnt","x":-110,"y":5238,"width":600,"height":70,"color":"4"}
	],
